WEBVTT

00:14.830 --> 00:15.790
You're lying!

00:16.140 --> 00:17.870
That can't be true!

00:24.170 --> 00:26.670
I lost my connection with Clayman.

00:27.260 --> 00:30.430
I viewed him as my own child,
but I couldn't sense him at all.

00:30.930 --> 00:35.180
I don't want to accept it,
but he's really dead.

00:38.430 --> 00:40.440
It's my mistake.

00:40.440 --> 00:42.520
I underestimated the Demon Lords.

00:42.520 --> 00:45.440
I should've been more careful.

00:45.440 --> 00:49.200
If you gonna put it that way,
I'm the one who suggested the idea.

00:49.550 --> 00:52.200
I never thought it'd
turn out like this, though.

00:52.590 --> 00:56.200
B-But I'm glad you made it back safely.

00:56.200 --> 00:59.710
Demon Lord Valentine was on par
with the president, right?

00:59.710 --> 01:01.330
How did you defeat him?

01:01.330 --> 01:05.630
We fought on the new moon when vampires
were at their weakest, after all.

01:05.630 --> 01:07.380
I was just lucky.

01:07.380 --> 01:12.050
Plus, I'm not as stupid as Clayman.

01:12.760 --> 01:15.390
Laplace! You shouldn't
speak of him like that!

01:15.760 --> 01:17.140
I'm only tellin' the truth.

01:17.140 --> 01:18.210
I warned him,

01:18.210 --> 01:21.890
but he got carried away even though
he was weak and died because of it.

01:21.890 --> 01:23.520
Laplace!

01:25.520 --> 01:28.990
What? You wanna go, Footman?

01:30.070 --> 01:32.030
Fine! Be my guest!

01:32.030 --> 01:33.820
Stop it, you two.

01:33.820 --> 01:35.490
We all feel the same.

01:35.910 --> 01:37.740
She's right, Laplace.

01:37.740 --> 01:41.250
Why are you playing the bad guy
all by yourself? That's not like you.

01:41.250 --> 01:46.250
I hired all of you. If anyone's gotta
be the bad guy, it should be me.

01:46.710 --> 01:48.800
That's what he was doing?

01:48.800 --> 01:51.050
My apologies, Laplace.

01:51.050 --> 01:53.300
Nah, that's fine.

01:53.300 --> 01:56.300
But it's not cool to blow
my act like that, y'know?

01:56.650 --> 01:59.220
I don't know
what exactly happened there.

01:59.220 --> 02:04.560
But as the Demon Lord Valentine put it,
Clayman definitely died.

02:04.940 --> 02:07.820
I wish I could have beaten it outta him.

02:08.210 --> 02:11.320
It's fine. I am glad that you
made it back safely, at least.

02:13.020 --> 02:15.820
But this is quite the conundrum.

02:16.170 --> 02:17.450
Yeah.

02:17.450 --> 02:23.790
We lost the base, forces, treasure, jewels,
and everything we gave Clayman.

02:23.790 --> 02:25.080
It's a staggering loss.

02:25.450 --> 02:27.210
Huh? What do you mean?

02:27.210 --> 02:32.510
Assuming the Demon Lords did kill Clayman,
shouldn't the base still be safe?

02:32.510 --> 02:37.680
His forces were routed,
but we can still make a comeback, no?

02:37.680 --> 02:40.640
That's what I called
you all here to discuss.

02:40.640 --> 02:45.690
Yesterday, the base I granted Clayman
fell in the course of a single evening.

02:45.690 --> 02:46.560
What?!

02:46.970 --> 02:51.940
What's shocking is that slime sent
a small group of his men to capture it.

02:51.940 --> 02:54.030
- No way!
- Impossible!

02:54.030 --> 02:57.740
So the Majins we saw on that battlefield
weren't even their full force?

02:57.740 --> 02:58.950
Right.

02:58.950 --> 03:04.620
That slime used the battlefield
as a diversion to strike the main base.

03:04.970 --> 03:09.750
Which is why I think we need
to look back at our plan.

03:09.750 --> 03:12.300
I think we need to be patient for now.

03:12.300 --> 03:15.760
If we want to achieve our goal
of conquering the world.

03:16.220 --> 03:17.590
I agree.

03:17.590 --> 03:21.390
Perhaps we got arrogant and tried
to bite off more than we could chew.

03:21.390 --> 03:22.910
Yep.

03:24.270 --> 03:28.560
I hate to say it, but being rash right now
is likely to make things even worse.

03:28.560 --> 03:32.860
I hesitate to accept it myself,
but I concede it is our best option for now.

03:33.230 --> 03:36.630
But still, it's no fun to be
the punching bag all the time, right?

03:37.090 --> 03:43.120
That slime took everything from Clayman,
so I think we should get back at him a bit.

03:43.120 --> 03:46.870
Huh? But didn't you say
we should lay low for the time being?

03:46.870 --> 03:50.250
Maybe we won't do anything,
but we can at least say something.

03:50.580 --> 03:52.170
What do you have in mind?

03:52.170 --> 03:55.760
Good grief, another one of your schemes?

03:56.660 --> 04:00.040
I say we should give him a little "poke."

04:17.490 --> 04:19.490
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

05:31.940 --> 05:35.480
HOLY EMPIRE OF LUBELIUS

05:35.980 --> 05:37.280
EPISODE 50: THE SAINT'S PLOY

05:37.280 --> 05:40.280
EPISODE 50: THE SAINT'S PLOY
The Holy Empire of Lubelius.

05:40.800 --> 05:43.780
This nation achieved
a completely equal society

05:43.780 --> 05:46.580
by entrusting everything to their god.

05:47.540 --> 05:54.290
And their god's true identity is none other
than the Demon Lord Luminus Valentine.

05:55.040 --> 05:57.550
The only person I have lost against.

05:58.460 --> 06:02.450
If you ever feel lost,
I want you to rely on me.

06:03.450 --> 06:05.970
Her way of doing things was too soft.

06:05.970 --> 06:06.910
And...

06:07.680 --> 06:11.430
If I keep relying on her,
I'll not be able to stand on my own.

06:12.340 --> 06:15.750
The only thing you can rely on
in this world is your own strength.

06:16.230 --> 06:18.190
And I've found it.

06:26.410 --> 06:28.950
The place that will make me stronger.

06:32.630 --> 06:37.130
I joined the Western Holy Church,
became a Paladin in my first year,

06:37.480 --> 06:40.130
and a Captain of the Crusaders
in my second year.

06:40.580 --> 06:45.760
But the higher I climb up the ladder,
the more I learn about the truth.

06:46.640 --> 06:48.890
And finally, I realized.

06:49.620 --> 06:54.350
That the Holy Emperor Lubelius
was actually a vampire named Louis,

06:54.350 --> 06:57.850
and a twin brother of
the Demon Lord Roy Valentine.

06:59.190 --> 07:04.780
Which means vampires claim
to be gods and rule over humans.

07:27.470 --> 07:30.720
Th-This is it for me, huh...

07:32.890 --> 07:37.520
But... I at least get rid
of the world of one evil...

07:42.150 --> 07:45.030
I could hear this racket
in my own bedchamber.

07:45.030 --> 07:47.030
What are all of you doing?

07:59.630 --> 08:04.470
I do not allow both of you to die
and leave me behind.

08:17.310 --> 08:19.310
You too, human.

08:20.310 --> 08:23.570
Don't die with that
misplaced pride in your mind.

08:27.860 --> 08:32.320
What is justice?
Is it about crushing evil?

08:32.720 --> 08:34.910
Assuming that it is,

08:34.910 --> 08:41.960
who do you think you are,
deciding whether I engage in evil or not?

08:42.380 --> 08:46.210
No justice can satisfy
all forms of free will.

08:46.650 --> 08:50.510
It is arrogant to think
you can do otherwise.

08:50.510 --> 08:51.840
Am I wrong?

08:53.890 --> 08:55.600
I'll give you a week.

08:56.190 --> 08:59.060
As you are powerful enough
to defeat my closest confidants,

08:59.060 --> 09:01.480
you can certainly overcome
the Seven Days Trial.

09:01.890 --> 09:05.730
Once you do, I will deign
to engage you seriously.

09:09.240 --> 09:13.490
I overcame the trial and faced
Lady Luminus one more time.

09:14.120 --> 09:16.910
And in where she defeated me,
I swore my loyalty to her.

09:20.250 --> 09:25.250
Lady Luminus and her kin don't actually
tear people apart to live off their flesh.

09:26.170 --> 09:30.720
They only needed a small amount
of blood to sustain themselves.

09:30.720 --> 09:35.760
And higher-ranked vampires could live for
eternity without even a need for blood.

09:36.760 --> 09:41.850
The happier the human are,
the tastier their blood will be,

09:41.850 --> 09:46.650
but Lady Luminus strictly forbids
any excessive extraction of blood.

09:47.320 --> 09:53.160
This nation's order and equality are high,
even among the Western Nations.

09:54.870 --> 09:59.180
Which is why I must protect
Lady Luminus no matter what.

09:59.790 --> 10:02.280
To protect this utopia.

10:04.420 --> 10:07.490
My brother, Lubel, died.

10:07.490 --> 10:08.990
You're joking, right?

10:08.990 --> 10:12.380
Roy was at the Walpurgis Council
as a Demon Lord, wasn't he?

10:12.900 --> 10:15.470
I'm telling the truth, Hinata.

10:15.470 --> 10:18.640
You knew that an intruder
got in last night, right?

10:19.200 --> 10:24.650
That intruder killed Roy who returned
early from Walpurgis Council and fled.

10:26.440 --> 10:27.440
I see.

10:27.940 --> 10:30.190
Roy was not weak.

10:30.190 --> 10:31.940
Although it was a false title,

10:31.940 --> 10:34.830
he's more than powerful enough
to be a Demon Lord.

10:35.490 --> 10:40.040
Which means that the clown
was stronger than a Demon Lord.

10:40.680 --> 10:42.120
But it should be no problem.

10:42.120 --> 10:45.420
As long as Lady Luminus is safe,
everything's fine.

10:45.420 --> 10:47.420
It is a problem, in fact.

10:47.420 --> 10:50.470
Now that Roy who we had
rampaging as a threat is dead,

10:50.470 --> 10:53.050
there is a chance people's faith
in our creed may dwindle.

10:53.800 --> 10:55.050
By the way.

10:55.510 --> 11:01.680
The Storm Dragon Veldora has been revived.
Yet, the Forest of Jura remains stable.

11:02.180 --> 11:03.210
Right.

11:03.680 --> 11:05.690
I don't know anything
about the evil dragon,

11:06.700 --> 11:12.320
but I imagine the forest is stable
because I let that slime, Rimuru, escape.

11:12.750 --> 11:17.490
I heard the Kingdom of Falmuth's
forces have been annihilated.

11:17.490 --> 11:19.580
Quite an adversary for you, wasn't he?

11:19.920 --> 11:23.580
Perhaps the moment I had him
encased in that Holy Field

11:23.580 --> 11:26.460
was the best chance
I had of defeating him.

11:26.810 --> 11:30.460
Did you give him some mercy because
he claimed to be from your realm?

11:30.880 --> 11:32.210
Of course not.

11:32.210 --> 11:36.080
Lady Luminus's aims do not align
with that slime's at all.

11:36.590 --> 11:40.970
That's why I ignored what he had to say
and tried to destroy his town.

11:41.410 --> 11:44.220
Because otherwise,
the angels will be moving soon, huh.

11:44.730 --> 11:45.510
Yes.

11:45.980 --> 11:50.310
If they keep developing the town
at that pace, they absolutely will.

11:50.310 --> 11:51.730
That would be distressing.

11:52.320 --> 11:56.650
I'd like to ensure that our victory
in the next Temma War is absolute.

11:56.650 --> 11:57.510
I know.

11:58.030 --> 12:00.990
That's why we can't afford
to speed up the timetable.

12:00.990 --> 12:06.750
But perhaps your failure
turned out well in the end.

12:07.180 --> 12:09.000
What do you mean?

12:09.350 --> 12:12.170
The Western Nations
will likely band together

12:12.170 --> 12:16.130
to deal with the threat emerging
in the Forest of Jura.

12:16.130 --> 12:22.260
With Roy gone, wouldn't they be a perfect
foe for humanity to unite against?

12:22.260 --> 12:25.020
I don't think it would work out
that nicely.

12:26.100 --> 12:29.520
It's preferable for us
if the Forest of Jura is stable,

12:29.520 --> 12:33.440
and if they sought to live alongside humanity,
that was all for the better.

12:34.160 --> 12:35.280
But...

12:35.900 --> 12:38.770
You know the Eastern merchant
who brought me information?

12:39.330 --> 12:41.530
We were planning to
meet last night as well.

12:41.530 --> 12:44.540
Oh? Rather good timing, then.

12:44.870 --> 12:49.000
Yes. That merchant
was trying to use me.

12:49.000 --> 12:54.000
If that were the case, then letting
Rimuru alive might be the right answer.

12:54.000 --> 12:55.420
Not to make excuses.

12:55.770 --> 12:58.340
Until we are fully ready,

12:58.340 --> 13:02.930
I say it's best to use that land
as a bulwark against the East.

13:03.420 --> 13:09.310
Assuming Rimuru survived
the Walpurgis Council, of course.

13:09.310 --> 13:12.940
Right.
Do you think he'll make it through?

13:12.940 --> 13:16.070
Lady Luminus will return soon.

13:16.070 --> 13:19.740
We will know by then.

13:19.740 --> 13:23.740
Having to tell her about your brother's
death is a depressing thought.

13:23.740 --> 13:25.410
She'll be in a bad state, I'm sure.

13:25.410 --> 13:28.700
Unlike me, she was a kind person.

13:29.910 --> 13:33.420
I suppose I'm not very kind myself.

13:33.420 --> 13:37.460
My own brother just died,
but I don't feel sad in the slightest.

13:44.350 --> 13:46.970
I see. So Roy is...

13:49.570 --> 13:50.980
What a stupid child.

13:52.270 --> 13:54.730
So what happened in Walpurgis Council?

13:58.870 --> 14:01.700
So that's what happened last night.

14:01.700 --> 14:05.700
That annoying evil dragon
just won't stop being in my way.

14:06.580 --> 14:08.120
And look at Roy, too!

14:08.660 --> 14:13.070
I could've revived him
if he was within my sight...

14:14.090 --> 14:15.830
I'm terribly sorry.

14:15.830 --> 14:18.380
All because I failed
to capture the intruder.

14:18.810 --> 14:19.960
So be it.

14:19.960 --> 14:23.050
You merely followed my orders.

14:23.050 --> 14:25.140
I am the one who deserves the blame.

14:25.570 --> 14:30.640
No, my lady. My brother simply
failed to meet your expectations.

14:30.640 --> 14:32.770
Please don't let it bother you.

14:33.520 --> 14:36.520
Now is not the time for us
to lament about our loss, huh.

14:37.510 --> 14:39.190
The evil dragon is revived,

14:39.190 --> 14:42.360
and a Demon Lord
by the name of Rimuru is born.

14:42.360 --> 14:44.680
We need to think of ways
to deal with them.

14:45.280 --> 14:48.240
- Yes.
- Understood, my lady.

14:48.240 --> 14:51.700
Allow me to defeat that Veldora for you.

14:53.080 --> 14:56.920
Hinata. You've certainly
gotten stronger.

14:56.920 --> 15:01.210
But Demon Lord Rimuru aside,
you're no match for Veldora.

15:01.650 --> 15:03.590
She's right, Hinata.

15:03.590 --> 15:06.720
That is how fearsome
a presence the dragon is.

15:07.430 --> 15:10.220
But he was sealed by a Hero, right?

15:10.220 --> 15:12.600
Listen, Hinata.

15:12.600 --> 15:15.480
That dragon is a form
of natural energy itself.

15:15.990 --> 15:20.570
Perhaps you could use magic
to quell a raging gale,

15:20.570 --> 15:23.490
but that dragon has its own free will.

15:23.960 --> 15:26.490
It cannot be cut with a sword
or affected by magic.

15:26.490 --> 15:30.740
The shock waves of his rampage
would simply ravage the land.

15:31.990 --> 15:33.750
It was truly a nightmare.

15:34.370 --> 15:39.750
That ever-so-beautiful Nightrose Castle
turned into a miserable pile of ashes...

15:40.200 --> 15:44.010
Even so, when it comes to it,
I will kill him.

15:47.340 --> 15:52.970
Hinata. I do not wish to lose you, too.
Restrain yourself.

15:52.970 --> 15:53.680
Yes, my lady.

15:54.600 --> 15:59.150
Seems like labeling Rimuru a monster
and ignoring his words was a mistake.

15:59.980 --> 16:04.490
I don't want to think that what I did
was wrong, considering my faith.

16:04.990 --> 16:09.070
But what if even that was what
that Eastern merchant wanted?

16:09.550 --> 16:11.090
How distasteful.

16:11.590 --> 16:13.830
Could it be they have
an informant of their own?

16:14.370 --> 16:17.960
Then, what should we do about
the new Demon Lord Rimuru?

16:17.960 --> 16:20.290
We have no choice
but to let him be.

16:20.290 --> 16:24.090
Fortunately, the Church hasn't declared
him a divine enemy yet, right?

16:24.590 --> 16:25.510
But...

16:26.090 --> 16:27.760
Is there a problem?

16:28.090 --> 16:31.390
I fear the city and highways
the monsters are building

16:31.390 --> 16:34.010
could accelerate the angels' invasion.

16:34.530 --> 16:37.020
Ah yes, there was that.

16:38.520 --> 16:41.020
Making the Demon Lord Rimuru
and the Storm Dragon Veldora

16:41.020 --> 16:44.400
our enemies would be unwise.

16:44.400 --> 16:47.320
And if they attract more attention for us,

16:47.320 --> 16:50.570
they might become the angels'
main target instead.

16:51.170 --> 16:53.580
Either way, there's no point
thinking about it now.

16:54.080 --> 16:58.250
But the existence of their town
could turn one of Luminism's core tenets

16:58.250 --> 17:02.210
of monsters being humanity's
common enemy on its head.

17:02.210 --> 17:06.590
How about we make him our accomplice
and have him serve as an evil Demon Lord for us?

17:07.010 --> 17:08.090
That could not happen.

17:08.450 --> 17:12.970
Rimuru said he wants to build
a nation where he can enjoy his life.

17:12.970 --> 17:15.720
He declared in front of all of us that

17:15.720 --> 17:18.600
he'd protect the humans
because he needed their help.

17:19.050 --> 17:20.560
Anyone who interferes with that,

17:21.010 --> 17:25.940
whether they're human, Demon Lord,
or Holy Church, is my enemy.

17:26.430 --> 17:27.400
So he said.

17:28.090 --> 17:30.570
If he doesn't already have
contact with the humans,

17:30.570 --> 17:32.990
we could've tried your idea, Louis.

17:32.990 --> 17:36.160
For now, then, all we can do
is sit and watch.

17:37.410 --> 17:42.120
Right. Simply hold ourselves as
we always do. No brash moves.

17:42.120 --> 17:44.880
Simply state the fact to our followers.

17:44.880 --> 17:47.920
That Veldora, the Storm Dragon, is back.

17:48.380 --> 17:51.430
And what about the Demon Lord Rimuru?

17:51.790 --> 17:57.180
Right. He seems the sort
who is open to political exchange.

17:57.180 --> 18:00.180
We could deceive the Western
Nations easily enough.

18:00.600 --> 18:02.370
Are you fine with that, Hinata?

18:02.370 --> 18:03.810
Understood.

18:03.810 --> 18:05.860
Would he bear a grudge against you?

18:05.860 --> 18:07.310
A little.

18:07.310 --> 18:09.820
I did try to kill him.

18:10.370 --> 18:12.240
Ah yes, you did.

18:12.240 --> 18:17.200
But Rimuru is not stupid enough
to make us his enemies.

18:18.230 --> 18:19.530
I will keep that in mind.

18:22.080 --> 18:28.750
Our nation will accept Tempest's
demand and pay for war reparations.

18:28.750 --> 18:32.840
It will be ten thousand stellars.

18:32.840 --> 18:37.350
Ten thousand stellars?!
That's equal to a million gold!

18:37.350 --> 18:39.220
We cannot accept that!

18:39.220 --> 18:43.100
Not to mention, we can't get that much
even if we emptied the national treasury!

18:43.100 --> 18:47.110
Indeed. We must resist
to the better end!

18:47.110 --> 18:49.150
With Veldora as our opponent,

18:49.150 --> 18:51.860
the Western Holy Church
will not stand by idly!

18:51.860 --> 18:54.610
I imagine that beauty Hinata
will take action.

18:54.610 --> 18:56.740
That vixen?

18:56.740 --> 18:58.030
Don't forget the Hero!

18:58.030 --> 19:01.620
Ah yes, "Lightspeed"
Masayuki of Engrassia!

19:01.970 --> 19:03.580
That's right.

19:03.580 --> 19:06.670
The strongest Hero of
them all who slew his foes

19:06.670 --> 19:09.250
before they even knew
what happened to them!

19:09.630 --> 19:14.720
Let's have him show Veldora that
Lightspeed is no mere nickname!

19:14.720 --> 19:19.260
Yes! That's the spirit! He'll exterminate
those monsters in the blink of an eye!

19:19.260 --> 19:21.850
The royal family must pay
for the reparations!

19:21.850 --> 19:24.850
We cannot accept any demand
from those monsters!

19:24.850 --> 19:28.270
Falmuth must resist with all their might!

19:28.940 --> 19:31.020
My brother... No, Your Majesty.

19:31.530 --> 19:35.780
Is a king as proud as yourself
truly admitting defeat so easily?

19:36.640 --> 19:38.820
Edward, listen to me.

19:38.820 --> 19:41.830
We are pitted against Veldora,
the Storm Dragon.

19:41.830 --> 19:46.290
My pride is a mere pile of ashes
compared with his tyranny.

19:46.630 --> 19:49.290
Are you not attempting to flee
by yourself?

19:49.290 --> 19:52.130
There is nowhere to flee to.

19:52.130 --> 19:57.800
That is exactly why I intend to pay
the reparations and abdicate the throne.

20:00.670 --> 20:02.890
If I do not abdicate,

20:02.890 --> 20:06.210
Falmuth will either become
their vassal state or continue the war.

20:06.210 --> 20:09.060
Are you all right with that?
It will mark the end of this nation.

20:09.400 --> 20:14.280
B-But simply surrendering
to this monster force...

20:14.280 --> 20:16.030
May I have a moment?

20:16.610 --> 20:20.490
I received these documents
in the morning today.

20:20.490 --> 20:25.700
Its content is so vital that I must
share it with all of you now.

20:27.610 --> 20:32.250
It is a declaration from
the Kingdom of Blumund.

20:32.670 --> 20:37.010
In it, they reaffirmed
their support for Tempest

20:37.010 --> 20:39.890
and criticized Falmuth's
failed campaign.

20:39.890 --> 20:42.470
Where does such a tiny kingdom
get the nerve?!

20:42.470 --> 20:45.350
They think they can enjoy
the last laugh, don't they?

20:45.350 --> 20:50.270
Blumund aside, it'd be very bad if
the Armed Nation of Dwargon made a move.

20:50.770 --> 20:54.650
Do you think King Gazel
will maintain his neutrality?

20:54.650 --> 20:58.240
No, the real issue is more
on the power of his words.

20:58.240 --> 21:03.530
As our vital trade partner,
it would be bad for us to anger their king.

21:05.240 --> 21:09.370
S-Sir! We've just received
an emergency report from the Guild!

21:09.370 --> 21:10.170
Give it to us.

21:10.170 --> 21:13.790
The monster Rimuru calming to be
the Chancellor of the Jura Forest

21:13.790 --> 21:15.800
just declared himself a Demon Lord!

21:16.180 --> 21:18.010
- What?!
- That is...

21:18.350 --> 21:20.260
It is in fact good news, no?

21:20.260 --> 21:22.680
The Demon Lords will
not take kindly to this.

21:22.680 --> 21:27.770
This overreaching Rimuru fellow will soon
learn the terror of true Demon Lords!

21:27.770 --> 21:32.770
I-If things go well, they might also
destroy Veldora along with him!

21:34.650 --> 21:38.570
Demon Lord Clayman has been
defeated by Demon Lord Rimuru!

21:38.570 --> 21:40.610
- What?!
- Nonsense!

21:40.610 --> 21:44.740
And Carrion and Frey have reportedly
renounced their seats as Demon Lords

21:44.740 --> 21:47.410
and affiliate themselves
with the Demon Lord Milim.

21:47.410 --> 21:51.710
The current eight members now
named themselves the Octagram!

21:54.670 --> 21:57.000
Did you hear that, everyone?

21:57.000 --> 22:01.590
Veldora is a threat, but this monster
Rimuru is another one entirely.

22:02.090 --> 22:05.850
He's a monster who could
easily beat Demon Lord Clayman.

22:06.200 --> 22:11.850
I proclaimed this was for our nation's sake,
but it was in fact my greed-driven mistake.

22:12.240 --> 22:14.400
I will leave my post as king.

22:14.400 --> 22:17.860
And I wish to nominate
Edward as my successor.

22:18.250 --> 22:19.150
Brother...

22:19.150 --> 22:23.320
- What?!
- Not Prince Edgar?

22:23.660 --> 22:27.120
We will face difficult times ahead.

22:27.120 --> 22:29.120
Edgar is still too young.

22:29.120 --> 22:31.830
He will have trouble overcoming any of it.

22:34.070 --> 22:38.170
I also believe that is our best option,
Your Highness.

22:44.090 --> 22:48.350
Thus, the great nation of Falmuth,
with all its long history,

22:48.350 --> 22:53.690
had signed an armistice
with the Jura Tempest Federation.

22:54.520 --> 23:01.940
With this, on the surface, Falmuth had
officially recognized Tempest as a nation.

24:36.500 --> 24:39.240
Next time, "Peaceful Days."
